  "description": "Modernize existing WinForms applications without rewriting them: a Tailwind-style styling layer for standard controls (and Krypton Toolkit with FormWind.Krypton). Utility classes with hover/focus/dark variants, ready-made looks (Fluent, Ant Design, Material) with AutoStyle, flex and grid layout, dark mode, DataGridView styling, lightweight charts and accessibility support. Known limitations: controls that paint themselves ignore FormWind's styles and may stay light in dark mode (owner-drawn grids can be inverted with TwGrid.EnableDarkInversion); the multi-line Classes editor window is available only in the .NET Framework Designer (the .NET 8+ Designer has the drop-down, smart tag and class builder).",
